这个异想天开的促销活动。

1211
00:56:39.720 --> 00:56:45.820
In the conference room, Michael is just like already taking credit for his great idea.
在会议室里，迈克尔就好像已经在为自己的好主意邀功了。

1212
00:56:46.100 --> 00:56:47.400
It's such a great idea.
这真是个好主意。

1213
00:56:47.660 --> 00:56:53.620
He needs everyone to come in the conference room and talk about how we need more good ideas like this one.
他需要每个人都进会议室，讨论我们如何需要更多像这样好点子。

1214
00:56:53.620 --> 00:56:57.260
He says, and this is like something, like people that do this crack me up.
他说，这就好像是某种，那种这样做的人让我觉得很好笑的事。

1215
00:56:57.340 --> 00:57:00.880
He goes, it might be the best idea ever in like the history of ideas.
他说，这可能是有史以来所有点子里最好的一个。

1216
00:57:01.040 --> 00:57:02.100
You're like, okay, buddy.
你就会想，好吧，老兄。

1217
00:57:04.380 --> 00:57:05.620
Here's what I don't understand.
我不明白的是这个。

1218
00:57:05.800 --> 00:57:10.960
He's written on a board, marketing, greatness, Michael.
他在白板上写了：市场营销、伟大、迈克尔。

1219
00:57:11.920 --> 00:57:12.960
I didn't get it.
我没搞懂。

1220
00:57:13.080 --> 00:57:14.320
It was very amusing to me.
我觉得这非常搞笑。

1221
00:57:14.320 --> 00:57:17.780
Well, his job is to profiligate great ideas.
好吧，他的工作就是大量涌现伟大的点子。

1222
00:57:18.040 --> 00:57:18.980
I guess so.
我想是吧。

1223
00:57:19.220 --> 00:57:22.580
He really wants the group, though, to tell them their golden ticket idea.
不过，他真的很想让大家把他们的金券点子说出来。

1224
00:57:22.740 --> 00:57:24.200
He knows his golden ticket.
他知道他的金券。

1225
00:57:24.560 --> 00:57:25.520
A golden ticket?
金券？

1226
00:57:25.680 --> 00:57:25.840
Yeah.
是啊。

1227
00:57:26.020 --> 00:57:27.800
Jim's like, well, we could rent out our trucks.
吉姆说，嗯，我们可以出租我们的卡车。

1228
00:57:27.880 --> 00:57:30.400
He's like, eh, no, Post-it notes, right?
他说，呃，不，便签纸，对吧？

1229
00:57:30.720 --> 00:57:31.340
Golden ticket.
金券。

1230
00:57:31.880 --> 00:57:34.880
NASA, lots of golden ticket ideas there.
美国宇航局，那里面有很多金券点子。

1231
00:57:35.800 --> 00:57:39.660
Andy's going to say golden girls and a few other things.
安迪打算说《黄金女郎》和其他一些事情。

1232
00:57:39.860 --> 00:57:41.160
That start with the word golden.
以“黄金”这个词开头的。

1233
00:57:41.160 --> 00:57:41.960
That start with golden.
以“黄金”开头的。

1234
00:57:41.960 --> 00:57:42.420
Golden graMs.
黄金麦片。

1235
00:57:42.420 --> 00:57:44.060
Look over his shoulder.
看他的肩膀后面。

1236
00:57:44.360 --> 00:57:46.540
Angela Martin, one minute, 59 seconds.
安吉拉·马丁，一分五十九秒。

1237
00:57:46.960 --> 00:57:48.400
Major eye roll at Andy.
对安迪翻了个巨大的白眼。

1238
00:57:48.900 --> 00:57:49.920
Angela eye roll?
安吉拉翻白眼？

1239
00:57:50.280 --> 00:57:50.580
Yeah.
对。

1240
00:57:51.020 --> 00:57:52.820
She thinks Andy's an idiot, guys.
她觉得安迪是个白痴，伙计们。

1241
00:57:53.740 --> 00:57:57.540
She was only engaged to him just two seconds ago, but she's over it.
她两秒钟前才刚跟他订过婚，但她已经不在乎了。

1242
00:57:58.060 --> 00:57:59.880
Well, now we're going to move to the kitchen.
好了，现在我们要转移到厨房。

1243
00:58:00.380 --> 00:58:02.440
Andy and Kevin are at the table.
安迪和凯文坐在桌子旁。

1244
00:58:03.020 --> 00:58:05.160
Pam and Jim are over by the counter.
帕姆和吉姆在柜台旁边。

1245
00:58:05.620 --> 00:58:08.600
And Kevin really wants to ask out Lynn.
凯文真的很想约琳。

1246
00:58:08.600 --> 00:58:12.520
And he's just getting a lot of advice from these guys.
而他正从这些人这里得到很多建议。

1247
00:58:13.240 --> 00:58:14.240
Conflicting advice.
互相冲突的建议。

1248
00:58:14.660 --> 00:58:17.700
I have two background catches that just delighted me.
我有两个背景镜头让我感到非常开心。

1249
00:58:18.140 --> 00:58:18.600
Oh.
哦。

1250
00:58:18.940 --> 00:58:19.560
All right.
好吧。

1251
00:58:19.820 --> 00:58:23.000
Number one, these guys are both eating donuts.
第一点，这两个家伙都在吃甜甜圈。

1252
00:58:23.480 --> 00:58:24.300
I noticed that.
我注意到了。

1253
00:58:24.400 --> 00:58:26.840
And I swear to God, those are the donuts we got every morning.
我向上帝发誓，那就是我们每天早上买的甜甜圈。

1254
00:58:26.900 --> 00:58:28.940
Because Kevin's donut is my donut.
因为凯文的甜甜圈就是我的甜甜圈。

1255
00:58:29.060 --> 00:58:29.980
The sprinkles donut.
那个撒了糖针的甜甜圈。

1256
00:58:30.160 --> 00:58:30.480
Yes.
没错。

1257
00:58:30.760 --> 00:58:32.280
And Andy had the powdered sugar.
而安迪吃的是糖粉的。

1258
00:58:32.900 --> 00:58:33.200
Okay.
好吧。

1259
00:58:33.580 --> 00:58:34.900
Background catch number two.
背景彩蛋之二。

1260
00:58:35.140 --> 00:58:36.760
I love it when our show does this.
我太喜欢我们节目搞这一套了。

1261
00:58:36.920 --> 00:58:41.840
When it takes an object from a prior episode and pops it back into a new one.
当它把前一集里的道具又塞进新一集里的时候。

1262
00:58:42.100 --> 00:58:42.280
Ready?
准备好了吗？

1263
00:58:42.760 --> 00:58:43.560
Four minutes.
四分钟。

1264
00:58:43.920 --> 00:58:45.040
I think I saw it too.
我想我也看到了。

1265
00:58:45.400 --> 00:58:46.540
Kevin's coffee mug?
凯文的咖啡杯？

1266
00:58:46.640 --> 00:58:46.960
Yep.
对呀。

1267
00:58:47.220 --> 00:58:52.020
Kevin's coffee mug is the same mug that Kelly gave to him at her customer survey party.
凯文的咖啡杯就是凯莉在她客户调查派对上送他的那个杯子。

1268
00:58:52.200 --> 00:58:54.340
You know, everyone's face in the big star.
你知道的，大星星上面印着每个人的脸。

1269
00:58:54.780 --> 00:58:56.560
But what about Andy's mug?
那安迪的杯子呢？

1270
00:58:57.340 --> 00:59:00.360
Andy's mug is the same one from Moroccan Christmas.
安迪的杯子是《摩洛哥圣诞节》里的同款。

1271
00:59:01.040 --> 00:59:03.820
And it was featured in a deleted scene I talked about.
而且它还出现在我聊过的一个被删片段里。

1272
00:59:03.980 --> 00:59:08.400
When Jim and Pam decide to shop within the office for Christmas for each other because
当时吉姆和帕姆决定在办公室里互买圣诞礼物，因为

1273
00:59:08.400 --> 00:59:12.220
they're so broke, Jim goes up to Andy and asks him about his mug.
他们太穷了，吉姆走到安迪面前向他打听他的杯子。

1274
00:59:12.700 --> 00:59:14.160
And it's in the bloopers.
这在NG镜头里也有。

1275
00:59:14.320 --> 00:59:15.360
It was also in the script.
剧本里也写了。

1276
00:59:15.780 --> 00:59:18.200
Two coffee mugs from two prior episodes.
来自前两集的两个咖啡杯。

1277
00:59:18.400 --> 00:59:19.020
I love that.
我太喜欢这样了。

1278
00:59:19.400 --> 00:59:24.060
Well, later in this episode, if you look at Oscar's desk, he's going to have his America's
对了，这集后面如果你看奥斯卡的办公桌，他也会用他那个《美国达人》的

1279
00:59:24.060 --> 00:59:25.080
Got Talent mug too.
杯子。

1280
00:59:25.500 --> 00:59:25.860
Ah!
啊！

1281
00:59:26.080 --> 00:59:26.640
Love it.
太棒了。

1282
00:59:30.360 --> 00:59:32.520
Much bigger in the actual shooting draft.
在实际的拍摄剧本里这个要宏大得多。

1283
00:59:32.700 --> 00:59:35.420
And there are a few deleted scenes and things I want to share.
还有一些被删片段和其他东西我想分享一下。

1284
00:59:35.760 --> 00:59:39.060
First of all, this is the scene that would have set up this whole storyline.
首先，这就是本来能铺垫整条故事线的那个场景。

1285
00:59:39.620 --> 00:59:42.560
It's at the beginning of the day and they're getting in the elevator.
那是天刚亮的时候，他们正在进电梯。

1286
00:59:43.000 --> 00:59:44.500
Kevin, Jim, and Pam.
凯文、吉姆和帕姆。

1287
00:59:44.760 --> 00:59:46.260
And who rushes in at the last minute?
谁最后关头冲了进来？

1288
00:59:46.380 --> 00:59:48.420
Because she works in the Scranton Business Park.
因为她在斯克兰顿商业园工作。

1289
00:59:48.760 --> 00:59:49.500
But Lynn.
是琳恩。

1290
00:59:50.000 --> 00:59:50.800
Can we hear it?
我们能听听吗？

1291
00:59:51.100 --> 00:59:51.940
Hold the mic, please.
请拿好麦克风。

1292
00:59:55.120 --> 00:59:55.720
Hi, Kevin.
嗨，凯文。

1293
00:59:56.600 --> 00:59:57.220
Hey, Lynn.
嘿，琳恩。

1294
00:59:58.200 --> 00:59:59.380
Did you get my message?
你收到我的消息了吗？

1295
01:00:00.340 --> 01:00:01.620
Um, yeah.
呃，收到了。

1296
01:00:02.140 --> 01:00:03.940
I've been really busy.
我最近真的很忙。

1297
01:00:05.140 --> 01:00:05.700
Oh.
噢。

1298
01:00:06.920 --> 01:00:07.620
It's okay.
没关系。

1299
01:00:08.500 --> 01:00:12.380
Yeah, I'm probably going to be busy for the next 20 days or so.
对啊，我大概在接下来的二十天左右都会很忙。

1300
01:00:15.520 --> 01:00:16.960
So, yeah.
所以，就这样吧。

1301
01:00:18.660 --> 01:00:19.080
Bye.
再见。

1302
01:00:21.200 --> 01:00:24.440
You're going to be busy for the next 20 days or so.
你接下来的二十天左右大概都会很忙。

1303
01:00:24.720 --> 01:00:25.980
I thought you liked Lynn.
我以为你挺喜欢林恩的。

1304
01:00:26.120 --> 01:00:26.940
I do like Lynn.
我是挺喜欢林恩的。

1305
01:00:27.460 --> 01:00:29.240
That's what Andy told me to say.
那是安迪让我这么说的。

1306
01:00:30.400 --> 01:00:31.360
Uh-huh.
呃-哈。

1307
01:00:32.220 --> 01:00:32.680
Right?
对吧？

1308
01:00:33.460 --> 01:00:39.140
So, Jim and Pam are learning that Andy has been giving Kevin some pretty bad advice.
所以，吉姆和帕姆发现安迪一直在给凯文出一些非常糟糕的主意。

1309
01:00:39.400 --> 01:00:39.740
Yeah.
是啊。

1310
01:00:39.960 --> 01:00:45.800
He likes Lynn but tells her, you know, he didn't return her messages and he's going to be busy for 20 days.
他喜欢林恩，却告诉她，你知道的，他没有回她的信息，而且他要忙上二十天。

1311
01:00:46.420 --> 01:00:46.940
Wow.
哇。

1312
01:00:47.900 --> 01:00:48.840
That's amazing.
这太惊人了。

1313
01:00:49.260 --> 01:00:51.840
Jim and Pam can't let Andy do this to Kevin.
吉姆和帕姆不能让安迪对凯文这么做。

1314
01:00:51.980 --> 01:00:53.420
So, they start giving him advice, right?
所以，他们开始给他出谋划策，对吧？

1315
01:00:53.540 --> 01:00:54.620
Just ask her out.
直接约她出去就行。

1316
01:00:54.620 --> 01:01:01.460
And in the deleted scenes, you really get a sneak peek into where Andy's brain is at.
而在删减片段里，你真的能一窥安迪心里到底在想什么。

1317
01:01:01.680 --> 01:01:03.000
You got to hear this talking head.
你得听听这段单采。

1318
01:01:03.340 --> 01:01:05.720
I was raised to be a gentleman around women.
我受到的教育是在女性面前要做一个绅士。

1319
01:01:05.880 --> 01:01:08.900
But when your fiancé is Satan, that doesn't work.
但当你的未婚妻是撒旦时，那一套就行不通了。

1320
01:01:09.240 --> 01:01:13.660
So, I have some new ideas and new techniques and I'm trying them out.
所以，我有了一些新想法和新技术，我正在尝试它们。

1321
01:01:14.140 --> 01:01:15.640
Kevin Malone is my guinea pig.
凯文·马龙就是我的小白鼠。

1322
01:01:16.580 --> 01:01:17.480
Aw, man.
天哪。

1323
01:01:17.480 --> 01:01:18.840
I wish that had stayed in.
我真希望这段能保留下来。

1324
01:01:19.020 --> 01:01:20.340
Doesn't that explain it all?
这不就全解释通了吗？

1325
01:01:20.340 --> 01:01:21.360
Well, it does.
嗯，确实。

1326
01:01:21.520 --> 01:01:30.020
I mean, I think I was able to realize that the reason that Andy is being this way is because he's still reeling from his breakup with Angela.
我是说，我觉得我能明白，安迪之所以会这样，是因为他还没从和安吉拉的分手中缓过来。

1327
01:01:30.240 --> 01:01:33.280
But that really would have been great.
但那段要是能播真的会很棒。

1328
01:01:33.480 --> 01:01:34.100
I know.
我知道。

1329
01:01:34.100 --> 01:01:37.160
Because, I mean, I don't think Andy's a bad guy.
因为，我的意思是，我不觉得安迪是个坏人。

1330
01:01:37.160 --> 01:01:40.700
But he's clearly hurt and acting out and using poor Kevin.
但他明显受了伤，在胡闹，还利用了可怜的凯文。

1331
01:01:41.120 --> 01:01:41.960
Well, listen.
好了，听着。

1332
01:01:42.440 --> 01:01:44.220
Jim's going to get a phone call now.
吉姆马上要接个电话了。

1333
01:01:44.760 --> 01:01:45.600
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

1334
01:01:45.860 --> 01:01:46.200
What?
什么？

1335
01:01:46.460 --> 01:01:49.380
His client, Tom, has found a golden ticket.
他的客户汤姆找到了一张金奖券。

1336
01:01:49.380 --> 01:01:52.220
Tom from Blue Cross of Pennsylvania.
来自宾夕法尼亚蓝色十字的汤姆。

1337
01:01:52.620 --> 01:01:53.580
Our biggest client.
我们最大的客户。

1338
01:01:54.140 --> 01:01:54.680
Uh-oh.
呃-哦。

1339
01:01:55.140 --> 01:01:57.540
Oscar, how much is that going to cost us?
奥斯卡，那会让我们损失多少？

1340
01:01:57.540 --> 01:01:58.800
Michael wants to know.
迈克尔想知道。

1341
01:01:58.980 --> 01:02:00.020
It's going to hurt a bit.
这会有点伤筋动骨。

1342
01:02:00.520 --> 01:02:02.200
Well, what about this?
那这个呢？

1343
01:02:02.680 --> 01:02:06.100
Guys, Tom found all five golden tickets.
伙计们，汤姆找到了全部五张金奖券。

1344
01:02:06.740 --> 01:02:07.900
Holy moly.
我的天哪。

1345
01:02:08.220 --> 01:02:10.380
Did they say one per customer?
上面写了每个客户限购一张吗？

1346
01:02:10.920 --> 01:02:11.180
Nope.
没有。

1347
01:02:11.260 --> 01:02:11.540
Nope.
没有。

1348
01:02:11.840 --> 01:02:17.420
Our biggest client just got 50% off their total order with us.
我们最大的客户在我们这儿的总订单直接打了五折。

1349
01:02:17.580 --> 01:02:19.060
I mean, this is a huge win.
我的意思是，这可是一次巨大的胜利。

1350
01:02:19.380 --> 01:02:20.880
Talk about winning the golden ticket.
这可真是中了金奖券了。

1351
01:02:21.100 --> 01:02:22.640
He won all the golden tickets.
他赢得了所有金奖券。

1352
01:02:22.660 --> 01:02:23.680
He won all of them.
他把所有的都赢了。

1353
01:02:24.120 --> 01:02:29.220
This made me think, Jenna, have you ever won like a really big ticket item?
这让我想知道，珍娜，你有没有赢过那种非常大件的奖品？

1354
01:02:29.680 --> 01:02:31.040
I don't think so.
我想没有吧。

1355
01:02:31.400 --> 01:02:36.480
I called my mom because I know my Aunt Anne has won things.
我打电话给我妈，因为我知道我阿姨安曾赢得过一些东西。

1356
01:02:36.660 --> 01:02:38.980
Like, she signs up for, you know, raffles and things.
比如，她会报名参加那种抽奖活动什么的。

1357
01:02:39.080 --> 01:02:40.200
And she's won trips.
而且她还赢过旅行。

1358
01:02:40.560 --> 01:02:41.000
Really?
真的吗？

1359
01:02:41.000 --> 01:02:42.380
Yeah, she's super lucky.
对啊，她运气超级好。

1360
01:02:42.680 --> 01:02:45.120
And I was like, Mom, doesn't Aunt Anne win a lot of things?
然后我就问：妈，安阿姨是不是赢过很多东西？

1361
01:02:45.180 --> 01:02:48.520
And she said, well, you know, your dad won a very big ticket item.
她说：哦，你知道的，你爸以前中过一个非常大件的奖品。

1362
01:02:49.300 --> 01:02:50.700
What did your dad win?
你爸赢了什么？

1363
01:02:50.860 --> 01:02:52.720
And I was like, Mom, what are you talking about?
我说：妈，你在说什么呢？

1364
01:02:52.800 --> 01:02:54.780
And she said, well, this was before you were born.
她说：哦，这是在你出生之前的事了。

1365
01:02:55.340 --> 01:02:57.740
And Jenna, this story just delighted me so much.
珍娜，这个故事真的让我太开心了。

1366
01:02:57.840 --> 01:03:00.420
One, because, you know, my dad's passed away.
第一，因为我爸爸已经去世了。

1367
01:03:00.520 --> 01:03:03.620
And so any new information, because, you know, you play every memory.
所以任何新的信息——因为你知道，你会反复回味每一个记忆。

1368
01:03:03.760 --> 01:03:04.420
You look at everything.
你会审视所有的事情。

1369
01:03:04.560 --> 01:03:09.240
But anything that you hear about someone you loved who's no longer with you, you just,
但任何关于你爱的人、那个已经不在你身边的人的听闻，你都会……

1370
01:03:09.460 --> 01:03:12.140
oh, it's like this beautiful, wonderful thing.
哦，这就好像是一件美好绝伦的事。

1371
01:03:12.140 --> 01:03:18.760
So my mom said, oh, yeah, before you were born, we had just moved to Lafayette, Louisiana.
所以我妈说：哦，对啊，在你出生前，我们刚搬到路易斯安那州的拉斐特。

